// Every local is lifted as an independent C object unless the frame layout
// says that loses something.  The serializer records each local's storage.
// When a local overlaps, or directly follows, a local whose address is taken,
// an access through that address reached it in the binary, so the lifter puts
// both in one backing array and reaches each through a view at its recovered
// offset.
//
// split_record, read_second and overlap are Ghidra's output for
//
//   struct pair { int a; int b; };
//   void split_record(int a, int b) { struct pair p = { a, b }; consume(&p); }
//   int  read_second(void)          { struct pair p; fill(&p); return p.b; }
//   int  overlap(int v)             { union { int i; char c[4]; } u; u.i = v;
//                                     fill(&u.c[1]); return u.i; }
//
// built for arm-none-eabi -mcpu=cortex-m3 -O1.  The decompiler splits `p` into
// two 4-byte locals at sp-16 and sp-12.  Lifted as two objects, clang -O2
// deleted the second store in split_record and returned undef from
// read_second; as one array both survive.  overlap has a single local and is
// left alone.
//
// piece_view is hand-written: `rec_lo` is a 4-byte view of the first half of
// the 8-byte `rec` (the shape Ghidra gives a field of a stack structure it
// tracks on its own) and shares its region.  `used` follows `rec` but is both
// written and read by the function, and `reg` lives in a register; both stay
// ordinary locals.
//
// misaligned is hand-written: `odd` is a 4-byte local one byte after the
// address-taken `tag`.  A typed view at that offset would be misaligned, so
// the two stay separate and the loss is reported: a warning by default, an
// error under -strict.
//
// RUN: bash %strip-json-comments %s > %t.json
// RUN: %patchir-decomp -input %t.json -emit-llvm -print-tu -output %t > %t.log 2>&1
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=WARN %s --input-file %t.log
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=C %s --input-file %t.c
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=LL %s --input-file %t.ll
// RUN: not %patchir-decomp -input %t.json -emit-cir -strict -output %t.strict > %t.strict.log 2>&1
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=ERR %s --input-file %t.strict.log
// RUN: test ! -e %t.strict.cir
